    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be a relation from the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to itself such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math>{<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;are prime numbers}. Then, the number of elements in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is"
  },
